### Bug Scenario and Root Cause

The bug report describes an issue with the `title` attribute being automatically added to `Menu.Item` components. This causes a tooltip to appear when hovering over menu items, which some users find undesirable. The images illustrate how the `title` attribute results in tooltips that display the full text of menu items, even when the text is truncated in the UI.

The root cause is that the `title` attribute is being set automatically, even when the `innerText` is identical to the `title`, which violates WCAG guidelines by creating redundant text. This is problematic for users who do not want tooltips to appear.

### Bug Location

The bug is located in the `src/menu/view/item.jsx` file, specifically in the `render` method where the `title` attribute is set using the `getTitle` method.

### Patch to Fix the Bug

To address this issue, we can modify the code to conditionally set the `title` attribute only when the `children` are not a pure string or when the text is truncated.

